{* ctools-attribution:begin (generated by scripts/sync_attribution.py; edit config/attribution.json)}{...}
{marker acknowledgments}{...}
{title:Acknowledgments}

{pstd}
{cmd:ccollapse} reimplements {cmd:collapse}, an official Stata command. Its
syntax, statistics, weights, storage types, labels, messages, and return codes
follow {cmd:collapse}.

{pstd}
{cmd:ccollapse} is pinned to this version of {cmd:collapse}:

{p2colset 9 27 29 2}{...}
{p2col:Command}{cmd:collapse} (official Stata){p_end}
{p2col:Authors}StataCorp LLC{p_end}
{p2col:Version}{cmd:collapse.ado} 6.2.2{p_end}
{p2col:Date}June 28, 2020{p_end}
{p2col:Header line}{cmd:*! version 6.2.2  28jun2020}{p_end}
{p2col:Shipped with}StataNow 19.5 (revision 14 Oct 2026){p_end}
{p2colreset}{...}

{pstd}
{cmd:ccollapse} follows {cmd:collapse} as it behaves in this Stata release.
{cmd:which collapse} shows the version of {cmd:collapse.ado} in your Stata.
{help ctools##acknowledgments:help ctools} lists the pinned versions of all
ctools commands.

{pstd}
Please report bugs and questions about {cmd:ccollapse} at
{browse "https://github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues":github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues}.
StataCorp does not support {cmd:ccollapse}. Undocumented differences between
{cmd:ccollapse} and {cmd:collapse} are bugs in {cmd:ccollapse}.

{pstd}
In this Stata release {cmd:collapse.ado} passes its arguments to
{cmd:collapse_17.ado} (version 1.1.0, August 17, 2022), which computes the
statistics with functions built into Stata. {cmd:ccollapse} follows the
results of that implementation. The definitions of the percentiles are those
of {cmd:summarize, detail} and {cmd:_pctile}.
{* ctools-attribution:end}{...}


